=== layout: one-panel

# Local Borders: Direct Attention

@body

## Cell overrides: solid, dashed, dotted, and no rule

{table-style=working border=none}
| Evidence | Interpretation |
| --- | --- |
| [Observed difference]{border-bottom="2pt solid accent"} | [Keep the measured result visible]{border-bottom="2pt solid accent"} |
| [Provisional model]{border-bottom="1pt dashed #24578F"} | [A hypothesis to test]{border-bottom="1pt dashed #24578F"} |
| [Next observation]{border-bottom="1pt dotted #24578F"} | [Collect more evidence]{border-bottom="1pt dotted #24578F"} |
| [No separating rule]{border=none} | [An open final row]{border=none background-color=#FFF2CC} |

=== layout: one-panel

# Cell Spacing: Align the Explanation

@body

## Local padding and vertical alignment inside one shared row

{table-style=working column-widths="1,1,1"}
| Top | Middle | Bottom |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [Start here]{vertical-align=top padding="8pt 14pt 20pt 5pt" border-left="2pt solid accent" border-top="1pt solid accent"} | [Read the full explanation before deciding whether the evidence supports the model.]{vertical-align=middle padding="8pt 12pt"} | [Then decide]{vertical-align=bottom padding-bottom=8pt padding-right=16pt border-right="2pt solid accent"} |

=== layout: one-panel

# Long Prose: Give Explanations Room

@body

## Explicit column proportions: narrow labels, generous explanations

{table-style=comparison column-widths="1,3"}
| Step | What you should check |
| --- | --- |
| Define H~0~ | State the expected relationship before inspecting the outcome. Use that model to predict the count in each category. |
| Compare | Match observed and expected categories. Keep units, labels, and the total sample size visible. |
| Interpret | Explain what the evidence says about the model. Connect the statistical result to a biological explanation. |

